gtk4, fyne and bubbletea draw `ui.tabs` as tabs, where each drew sngl:ui's row
of buttons over the panels. gtk4's is a `Tabs`, the runtime's GtkNotebook in
a box (`cgo.SnglTabsNew`), and each tab a `TabPage` the notebook holds;
fyne's is fynelayout.NewTabs, an AppTabs, with a fynelayout.TabPage per tab;
bubbletea's is a row of focusable `Styled` labels in tui.TabLook's boxes over
the panels' box. Every panel is still mounted with the tabs and hidden while another is
selected.

The page is what a test presses: its `@change` writes `selected` and emits
the tabs' `change(k)`, which is what lower.NamePresses looks for, and is named
for that event so the press and the invoker each target writes for it agree.
gtk4's tabs and fynelayout fire it only when the user, not the program,
changes the page shown. A tab an `if` writes reaches the notebook, or the
AppTabs, through the render slot's insert into the tabs, and leaves through
its remove.

`cmd/sngl/testdata/tabs_look_runs.txt` runs it, gtk4's in Go and in C.

deny out/go/gtk4/main.go `"GtkButton"` -- a tab is a page of the notebook, which draws its tabs
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `widget.NewButton` -- a tab is an AppTabs item

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import "sngl:test"

component strip ui.node {
    var idx = 0
    var changed = -1
    var extra = false

    ui.tabs #tabs(:selected=idx, style={padding=8px}, @change(i) {
        changed = i
    }) {
        ui.tab(label="One") {
            ui.text(value="first panel")
        }
        ui.tab(label="Off", disabled=true) {
            ui.text(value="second panel")
        }
        if extra {
            ui.tab(label="More") {
                ui.text(value="more panel")
            }
        }
    }
}

func testPressingATabSelectsIt(t test.Test, c strip) {
    c.extra = true
    c.tabs.change(2)
    t.assert(c.idx == 2)
    t.assert(c.changed == 2)
}

ui.window(title="t") {
    strip
}

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
}
